Notes:
The attempts counter is calculated by ATM to reduce work for CO (By very little!).

Assumptions about under-lying protocols:
  All the messages between client and server reach their destinations without fail on the first try (No loss, No corruption, No duplication).

Flaws identified:
  If the user ends the session before the card is blocked and scans it again, he/she gets X amount of chances once again.
  No check to verify if the cash is dispensed and received by the user.
  The handshake shouldn't be part of the applicatiion-layer protocol.

Open Questions:
  What happens when a message fails to reach destination?
  How to verify if the client is legitimate (A host acting as an ATM/CO case) End-point Authentication?
  How's CIA achieved? Data is prone to sniffing!
